;; Lib/test's language-core methods pyi does not run as CPython 3.14.10 does (bin/pyi lib-test, test/python/libtest_judge.ae;
;; queue 194, PY6a), each in a class. :classes: each class's title, kind (:design, by design; :deferred, an owner's
;; work), owner (the milestone whose files it waits on), why, where it was decided, and :match, the regexes the
;; writer classes a new method's line by ("import MESSAGE", "stopped-in MESSAGE", "crash MESSAGE", or pyi's
;; "OUTCOME REASON"). :methods: every method not equal, "MODULE/TEST-ID" -> its class, written by
;; bin/pyi lib-test --record (a method's class kept, else the first class whose :match finds its line; a method of no
;; class is printed, left out and the run exits 3: no placeholder class is written, as CS265 (a) and CS266 (a)'s
;; writers). The judge passes a method that is not equal only when :methods names it with a class of :classes.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:ast-objects
  {:title "compile() to and from AST objects"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY9"
   :why "compile(..., ast.PyCF_ONLY_AST) returns a code object, and compile() of an ast.Module refuses it: _ast's node classes exist (PY6a) but the bridge between Python forms and ast objects is the native reader's (survey §6.6: \"_ast (Python forms <-> ast objects: the bridge that makes ast.parse inside pyi the native reader)\")"
   :decided "survey §6.6, PYS4; the user, 2026-11-03 (PY9 beside PY6)"
   :match [#"^failure <class 'code'> != <class 'ast\.Module'>" #"compile\(\) arg 1 must be a string, bytes or AST object" #"'code' object has no attribute 'body'"]}
  :code-positions
  {:title "code objects' line table and positions (PEP 626, PEP 657)"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY5b"
   :why "pyi's IR keeps a line per instruction but not CPython's line table: the line events and f_lineno of PEP 626's cases (after a raise in except, finally, with), co_positions and co_lines"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9 (PY5b: the compiler and code.go); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match [#"'code' object has no attribute 'co_positions'"]}
  :codecs
  {:title "codecs and Unicode errors beyond utf-8, ascii and latin-1"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY6c"
   :why "_codecs has utf-8, ascii and latin-1 (PY6a); the other codecs (cp437 ...) and UnicodeEncodeError's and UnicodeDecodeError's own str and attribute checks are the text family's"
   :decided "PY6a's proposed split (PY6c, text); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match [#"unknown encoding: "]}
  :compiler-errors
  {:title "a SyntaxError CPython's compiler or parser raises that pyi's does not, or raises in other words"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY5b"
   :why "pyi's compiler (arbace.python.compile) and the reader's errors miss some of CPython's compile-time checks (mapping keys and value patterns that are not literals, starred type-variable defaults, nonlocal of a type parameter, async comprehensions outside async functions) or word them otherwise (f-string assignment and deletion targets, an unterminated triple-quoted f-string's text); the messages of the parser are the native reader's (PY9) once it reads"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9 (PY5b: the compiler's fixes the runs find); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match []}
  :compiler-warnings
  {:title "the reader's SyntaxWarnings"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY9"
   :why "the tokenizer's and parser's SyntaxWarnings (an invalid escape sequence in an f-string, a numeric literal followed by a keyword) are CPython's parse in the helper (tools/pydump), which does not pass them on; the native reader's (PY9) to make; the compiler's own (assert of a tuple, is with a literal, a missed comma) are pyi's since queue 200 (PY6-core)"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9; survey §11 (PY9: the native reader); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match [#"^failure SyntaxWarning not triggered"]}
  :coroutines
  {:title "coroutines' attributes and the generator-based coroutine"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY5d"
   :why "coroutine objects lack cr_frame, cr_code and cr_origin, types.coroutine's generators (CO_ITERABLE_COROUTINE) cannot be awaited, anext is missing, and the async with and async for paths word some errors otherwise or let an exception through"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9 (PY5d: coroutines); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match [#"'coroutine' object has no attribute 'cr_" #"'generator' object can't be awaited" #"name 'anext' is not defined" #"get_coroutine_origin_tracking_depth"]}
  :cpython-only
  {:title "@cpython_only and check_impl_detail() tests skip under pyi"
   :kind :design
   :owner "none (by design)"
   :why "sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\", so test.support's cpython_only and check_impl_detail() skip the tests of CPython's implementation details, as PyPy runs Lib/test; CPython runs them"
   :decided "PYS15 (a)"
   :match [#"^skipped implementation detail specific to cpython"]}
  :docstrings
