   :decided "survey §1 and §14; PYS15 (a)"
   :match [#"don't know how to disassemble code objects"]}
  :exc-state
  {:title "the exception state of handlers and generators, and implicit chaining"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY5d"
   :why "sys.exception() and __context__ as CPython keeps them per frame and per generator: a generator's saved exception after it is closed, thrown into or resumed, the context a raise inside a handler sets (KeyError's, a cycle not made), the context left after an except clause"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9 (PY5d: generators, except); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match []}
  :finalization
  {:title "finalization: __del__ and weak references at the point CPython's reference counting runs them"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY7"
   :why "pyi's objects are Go's, collected by Go's collector: __del__ and weakref callbacks do not run when the last reference goes (an object a frame or exception held is still alive after gc_collect), the unraisable hook is not called from them; survey §6.5 (PYS9): a class measured at PY7"
   :decided "PYS9; survey §6.5"
   :match [#"'NoneType' object has no attribute 'err_msg'"]}
  :pattern-captures
  {:title "a pattern's captures stored as they match, not when the whole pattern has"
   :kind :deferred
   :owner "PY5d"
   :why "CPython's codegen keeps a pattern's captured values on the stack and stores the names only when the whole case pattern matches (pattern_context's stores); pyi stores each name as its sub-pattern matches, so a failed alternative or case leaves names bound"
   :decided "PYI-SPEC.md §9 (PY5d: match); the user, 2026-11-03 (PY6a's exit)"
   :match []}
